      <Layer queryable="1">
        <Name>7</Name>
        <Title><![CDATA[BOEM Limit of OCSLA 8(g) zone]]></Title>
        <Abstract><![CDATA[The  Outer Continental Shelf Lands Act '8(g) Zone' lies between the Submerged Lands Act (SLA) boundary line and a line projected 3 nautical miles seaward of the SLA boundary line. Within this zone, oil and gas revenues are shared with the coastal state(s). The official version of the ‘8(g)’ Boundaries can only be found on the BOEM Official Protraction Diagrams (OPDs) or Supplemental Official Protraction described below.]]></Abstract>
